WEBVTT

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.920
<i>Hey, Kuro!</i>

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.810
<i>Over here.</i>

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.990
<i>Yoohoo.</i>

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:23.990
<i>You—</i>

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.660
What do you want?

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.130
Could you stop being so conspicuous?

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.540
<i>So scary.</i>

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.350
<i>I'm at the mysterious item shop right now.</i>

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.510
Mysterious item shop?

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.200
You mean mysterious items like Shoji Vision,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.080
the Teapot of Loose Lips, and that 
furoshiki cloth from the other day?

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.110
<i>Yeah, it's a shop that buys and 
sells those kinds of products.</i>

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.890
<i>If you want to come, I'll have my 
little Moke-chan show you the way.</i>

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.150
<i>What'll it be?</i>

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.200
I'm on my way.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:24.430
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
<b>Episode 3 "Mysterious Item Shop Akatsuki"</b>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Akatsuki

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.880
Hey, Kuro. You made it!

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:38.490
I'll buy you a snack.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.430
I recommend this.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.320
Let's split one.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.010
Hello.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.380
You're Ramu-chan's assistant, Kuro-kun?

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.450
I'm the shopkeeper here. My name is Nico.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.140
Nice to meet you.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.990
Likewise.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.600
Excuse me.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.390
152 centimeters.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:03.340
Your voice sounds calm and even, 
but are you a grade school student?

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:07.660
Kuro, he called you a grade school student!

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.110
Ow!

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.200
I'm in <i>middle school</i>.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.880
Oh, sorry. I meant no offense.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.490
Doctor, I came because I heard 
this was a mysterious item shop.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.010
Huh? That's exactly what it is.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.270
It feels like an antique shop.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.040
Yeah.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.080
Sometimes customers mistake us for one.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.540
I made tea.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.390
When's Granny coming back?

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:01.310
Soon, probably.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.510
Granny?

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.220
This old lady who knows tons
 about mysterious items.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.630
She ran this shop till she turned 103.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.530
I'm still only half the shopkeeper she was.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.900
She handles the buying and 
selling of mysterious items.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.020
She sounds rather long-lived.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.850
She's still working?

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:20.910
Huh?

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.770
Welcome back,

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.660
Grandma.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.440
What?

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.260
Hey, Granny. I've been waiting for you.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.170
Ramune, you're here?

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.430
It's good to see you again.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.780
Is that boy your assistant?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.040
This is former shopkeeper Granny Ayame.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.350
Despite her looks, on the inside 
she's a total of 112 years old.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.300
Total?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.430
She has memories of her past life.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:54.320
If you bothered to wait for me, then you 
must be looking to buy a mysterious item.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:55.810
What do you want?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.200
Another Shoji Vision set.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.090
Kuro, you seem rather 
fascinated by all of this.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:04.970
That interesting, huh?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.450
I didn't know mysterious items were made.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:12.240
There's a wide variety of items, but 
they can't be made by just anyone.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.580
Granny Ayame's only able to make them 
because of her 112 years of knowledge—

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:20.970
Goodness, Ramune, I think that's 
enough mentions of my age.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.970
Oh? I'm missing an ingredient.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:24.950
Huh?

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.180
Can't be helped.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.820
I won't be able to finish today.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.330
Seriously?

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:36.890
Kuro, here. Take half.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.210
This half's mine.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.220
Is there a difference?

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:42.470
There's totally a difference.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:44.320
They're completely different.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.360
Hey.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.190
Is there someone there?

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.780
Hey, who are you?!

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.370
How long have you been standing there?!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:01.210
What? I was out there calling 
for someone for a while.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.580
I came inside because nobody answered.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.240
How can I help you?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.950
This is an antique shop, right?

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.420
I thought I'd sell these to you.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:13.950
Oh, really?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.020
Grandma?

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.230
There's a mysterious item mixed in here.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.860
By the way,

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.630
I really want that.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.430
You can't have this.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.110
I see. That's too bad.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.600
In that case, you will be missed.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:53.470
<b>You will be missed</b>

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:01.220
Ramune, I'm not sure if 
you're lucky or unlucky.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.850
Where did that come from?

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:08.600
That man had the ingredient I was 
missing for your Shoji Vision.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:09.620
Huh?

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:11.490
But he wouldn't sell it to me.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:12.610
What?

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.990
He's probably a burglar.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:15.880
What?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:26.750
<b>Takada Antiques</b>

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:26.750
Do Not Enter

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:21.140
There's been a burglar in the neighborhood
 lately who only targets antique shops.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:24.640
Nobody could figure out how he was 
getting in without breaking the locks.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.750
The police were stumped.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:31.640
But if he's using a mysterious 
item, that would explain it.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:35.250
That man had a Cattail Flower.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.270
What's that?

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.980
It's a mysterious item that turns you 
invisible when you put it in your mouth.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.840
The cost is your presence.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.270
Your presence?

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:52.490
Remember how nobody noticed him 
when he entered the shop just now?

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.370
If you use it too much,

00:07:54.370 --> 00:08:00.030
people stop noticing you even when you 
don't have the cattail in your mouth.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.880
You might as well be dead.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.240
Well, no matter.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.690
Vanishing because 
a mysterious item used you

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.770
is the perfect end for a burglar.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.210
Where are you going, Doctor?

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.180
What a softie.

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:38.890
Doctor, don't take off like that.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:40.040
Oh, sorry.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.590
Are you going after him?

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:45.670
Yeah, but his presence is disappearing.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.300
If he's hard to spot with our eyes, 
we'll have to use our heads to find him.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.020
He still had other antiques on him.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.940
He'll probably go to other 
shops to sell them.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:57.460
Are there any antique shops around here?

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.960
I see. Kuro, you're so smart!

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:03.340
There's a shortcut through that park!

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.650
So, what are we going to do, Grandma?

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.610
Well...

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:23.040
Dangerous mysterious items seduce people.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.580
You don't use them.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.170
They use <i>you</i>.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:36.080
Why don't we see how they handle this?

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:46.240
Hey, you.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:50.430
Give me that thing hanging from your neck.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.940
You can't have this.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.890
The jig is up!

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:59.000
You've been using that to shoplift, right?

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.490
You really shouldn't!

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.650
I doubt you know, but using that thing 
gradually erases your presence.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.420
Ultimately, you—

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.780
I know.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.370
I knew, and used it anyway!

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.200
I'm such an idiot.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.260
Just a little.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.300
I thought I'd be fine to 
use it just a little more!

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.500
But I'm already starting to disappear!

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.310
Hey.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.820
Help me!

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.020
If you want to be saved, hand it over.

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:36.530
Name your price.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.300
What? I didn't say that.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:42.200
What? You're not making any sense.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.080
<i>Has the mysterious item taken over his mind?</i>

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.850
I finally escaped.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:51.330
I'm not being sealed away again.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:57.340
I need to build up my strength by 
consuming the presence of humans.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.990
Can I eat you, too?

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:05.150
If you want it that badly, let's make a bet.

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:08.640
Grandma Ayame, Nico-nii.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.660
We'll give you the presence 
of all four people here.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.390
If you win our wager, that is.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:19.440
Four people, huh? A tasty offer.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:23.190
But there must be something you want, too.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.650
Of course.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:29.380
First, I want your Cattail Flower.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:34.410
Second, I want you to return that 
man's presence that you consumed.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:35.820
That's all?

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:39.180
These hardly seem like even terms.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:40.500
It's all right, Kuro.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:43.750
Granny only takes bets she can win.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:47.770
Give how sweet the deal is for 
him, he's sure to accept.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.170
Very well.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:52.200
However, I'll decide what we'll bet on.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:53.360
I choose hide and seek.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.730
We'll play within this park.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.410
First, I'll have 100 seconds to hide.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:04.870
Then each of you will have one minute to 
look for me, for a total of four minutes.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:08.900
If any one of you finds me, you win.

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:11.120
If you can't, I win.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:14.000
No. You have too much of an advantage.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.440
If you won't accept my conditions, 
then the bet's off.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.110
Fine. Let's do it.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:27.380
Then get ready for me to win.

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.300
You all, too.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.410
He marked us with blood?

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:38.890
Blood is what binds participants
 to magic rituals.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:40.700
He's preventing us from escaping.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:45.470
We just have to do the same 
thing when we find him.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:58.210
Do you know why it's forbidden to 
play hide and seek after dusk?

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:04.230
Because you'll be spirited 
away once you lose to me.

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:05.150
What?

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:10.180
Let's get this game of 
hide and seek started.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.800
He really turned invisible.

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.220
What? This can't be legal.

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.310
There's no time.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:22.210
What's our order?

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.400
I'll go first.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.230
Kuro.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:29.020
Ramune, you'll go second.

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:30.730
I'll go after you.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.810
I can't let my cute 
great-grandchild go first.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.050
Thank you, Grandma.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:41.430
Sorry.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:45.260
I got everyone caught up in this 
because I acted without thinking.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.320
It's too late for that.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:51.500
I'm used to your eccentricity.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:55.020
I don't pick fights I can't win.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:58.520
I'm excited for this game of 
hide and seek, Ramu-chan.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.910
Guys...

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.480
When we vanish, we vanish together!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.070
Why are you being such a coward?

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.920
Didn't I say we're going to win?!

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:13.160
It's been 100 seconds. I'm going.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.110
Good luck, Kuro!

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:16.160
Shut up.

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:19.620
<i>Randomly searching for 
him is a waste of time.</i>

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:23.970
<i>Based on the way he spoke, 
he's confident he'll win.</i>

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:29.420
<i>Someone that confident wouldn't 
choose a standard hiding spot.</i>

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.410
<i>He'll hide someplace provocative.</i>

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:39.890
Hey, Kuro!

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:41.140
Quit playing around!

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:43.270
There's a lot of playground equipment here.

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.350
He's searching all the exhausting 
hiding places first.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.700
Oh, I see.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:50.230
I thought he was just having fun.

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:55.990
Doctor, your turn.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:56.710
Got it.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.950
<i>I'm the one who got everyone 
caught in this mess.</i>

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:05.240
<i>I've gotta be the one to find him!</i>

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:10.840
Sorry, Granny.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:11.990
What are you, an old man?!

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:14.980
It's pretty hard to run for a whole minute.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:16.810
No matter.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:20.220
I never expected you to find him.

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:22.220
Didn't I tell you?

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:25.220
I don't pick fights I can't win.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.420
Isn't that...

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.740
A Lattice Fox.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.340
It allows you to see all things inhuman—

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:34.720
be they fox demons or "the mysterious"—
when you look through it.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.360
There's no rule against using 
mysterious items in hide and seek.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:42.640
She expected this to happen.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:43.870
But it won't work.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:47.600
If that's why she thought 
we'd win, we're gonna lose.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:01.940
Why?

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.870
Why can't I see anything?

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:08.290
Why will we lose?

00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:11.020
Because it's a <i>human</i> who's hiding.

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:14.080
The Lattice Fox won't show anything.

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:17.360
What are we going to do, Granny?!

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:21.000
Doctor.

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:42.010
<i>I won. I won. I won!</i>

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.640
<i>That just leaves...</i>

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:49.390
I'm sorry.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.490
I couldn't find him.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.560
You've got some other goal here, don't you?

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:05.410
That's surprisingly 
insightful of you, Ramune.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.770
Well, yeah... I guess so.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:12.080
I didn't think it was possible 
for someone who knows

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.440
so much about mysterious 
items to make that mistake.

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:17.210
Oh, I see. It was you.

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:21.680
I wanted to make this louder.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.960
That's it.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.070
Nico-nii.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.820
You can count on me.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.730
Nico-nii, you can do it!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.890
Shut up. He won't be able to hear it.

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:37.250
Hear it?

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:40.830
Your heart rate increases 
when you're excited.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:46.390
After seeing my strategy fail, 
he's certain he'll win.

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:49.330
I made the sound of his heart louder.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.830
But how will that help us find—

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.340
Nico-nii is blind.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.460
What?

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:04.720
He sees with all of his other senses.

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.730
He uses echos to determine the position 
and distance of objects around him.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:12.370
He can accurately determine what 
they are just by touching them.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:14.850
His sense of smell and taste 
are exceptional, too.

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:17.220
Not only that, but he can even 
detect "the mysterious."

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:20.370
Nico-nii's senses are superhuman.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:25.590
He can't see, but he "sees" 
better than anyone else.

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:29.510
<i>One heart rate is faster than the others.</i>

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.010
<i>It's nearby.</i>

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:36.340
<i>Ah, this is...</i>

00:18:47.170 --> 00:18:48.350
Found you.

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:56.150
That's impossible!

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.980
Nico-nii, nice one!

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:12.260
I can't believe he was hiding so close.

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:14.920
Impressive as always, Nico. Thank you.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.750
No, it's thanks to all of you.

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:22.190
The area I had to search was narrowed 
down because Kuro-kun ran so much.

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:25.590
Grandma made him easier to find by sound.

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:27.900
Nico-nii,

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:29.620
what about me?

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.920
Thanks for your moral support.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.650
Now then.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.770
I won our bet.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:51.070
It's time to return that man's presence.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:55.340
Akatsuki

00:19:58.660 --> 00:19:59.990
Here. This is for you.

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:01.980
Thanks, Granny!

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:03.050
No problem.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:06.000
I'll be sending you a huge bill 
for all the trouble you caused.

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:10.350
Just how much had you already 
accounted for this time?

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:12.420
All of it, of course.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:14.480
Make your opponent believe 
he has the advantage

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.880
and bait him into a situation 
advantageous for yourself.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.860
It's a standard tactic in negotiations.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.760
<i>She </i>has<i> been alive for 112 years, huh?</i>

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:25.610
<i>Some random brat could never beat her.</i>

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:27.650
Let's go home.

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:30.130
Since we worked up a sweat, 
let's stop by a public bath.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:33.400
Nico-nii, lend me some clothes.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:35.450
Sure. Kuro-kun?

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:36.820
Yes, please.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.230
I'm in <i>middle school.</i>

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:45.060
Oh, sorry. I meant no offense.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:46.100
Um...

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.310
Will my clothes fit you?

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.980
Maybe Grandma's clothes will fit you better?

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:56.610
Yeah, why don't you do that?

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:59.010
Borrow something frilly.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:02.740
Akatsuki

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.260
Ow!

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:06.500
Later, Granny and Nico-nii.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:10.230
Sorry for all the trouble he caused.

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:11.690
See you later.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:17.780
Ramune still has a lot to learn.

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:20.430
He's nothing like his sadistic master.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:25.490
He's got potential, though.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:28.830
I'm a genius.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:32.450
If we use this Cattail Flower, we can 
enter the women's bath all we want.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:35.190
I hope you vanish with 
the rest of the bubbles.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.020
What?

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:20.250
Binder Clip

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:21.750
Binder Clip

00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:29.240
<i>Doctor, our patient's fingertips 
have turned into chili peppers.</i>

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:32.760
<i>What? Then we can make all 
the mapo tofu we want.</i>

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:34.010
<i>You're going to make me mad.</i>

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:35.780
<i>"</i>Dr. Ramune -Mysterious 
Disease Specialist-<i>."</i>

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:38.860
<i>Episode 4, "Chili Pepper Fingertips."</i>

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Episode 4 
